1. Use string function to perform the following:
     Take 2 variables one for Language and 1 variable for Tamil.
     The result should display as "LANGUAGE: Tamil"

SET @lan1 = 'Language';
SET @tam1 = 'Tamil';

SELECT CONCAT(UPPER(@lan1), ': ', @tam1) AS Result;

2. Extract the day,month & year from today's date and print it in seperate columns like DAY, MONTH and YEAR
SELECT DAY(CURDATE())   AS DAY,MONTH(CURDATE()) AS MONTH,YEAR(CURDATE())  AS YEAR;
